===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*men- (stand out)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mouth}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mūþ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*munþ}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*munþaz|t=mouth}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ment-|t=to chew; jaw, mouth}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|mooth||mouth}}, {{cog|frr|müd}}, {{m|frr|müth}}, {{m|frr|müss||mouth}}, {{cog|fy|mûn||mouth}}, {{cog|nl|mond||mouth}}, {{m|nl|muide||river mouth}} and {{m|nl|mui||riptide}}, {{cog|de|Mund||mouth}}, {{cog|sv|mun||mouth}}, {{cog|no|munn||mouth}}, {{cog|da|mund||mouth}}, {{cog|fo|muður}}, {{m|fo|munnur||mouth}}, {{cog|is|munnur||mouth}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌿𐌽𐌸𐍃||mouth}}, {{cog|la|mentum||chin}} and {{m|la|mandō||to chew}}, {{cog|grc|μάσταξ||jaws, mouth}} and {{m|grc|μασάομαι||to chew}}, {{cog|sq|mjekër||chin, beard}}, {{cog|cy|mant||jawbone}}, {{cog|hit|||tr=mēni|chin}}. The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|mouthen}}, from the noun.

[[File:Mouth illustration-Otis Archives.jpg|right|thumb|An illustration of the inside of a human mouth, with cheeks cut and lips pulled back.]]

