===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[opening]] of a [[creature]] through which [[food]] is [[ingest]]ed.
#: {{ux|en|"Open your '''mouth''' and say 'aah'," directed the doctor.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=7|passage=I made a speaking trumpet of my hands and commenced to whoop “Ahoy!” and “Hello!” at the top of my lungs. {{...}} The Colonel woke up, and, after asking what in brimstone was the matter, opened his '''mouth''' and roared “Hi!” and “Hello!” like the bull of Bashan.}}
# The end of a [[river]] out of which water flows into a sea or other large body of water.
#: {{ux|en|The '''mouth''' of the river is a good place to go birdwatching in spring and autumn.}}
# An [[outlet]], [[aperture]] or [[orifice]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1764|author=Horace Walpole|title=The Castle of Otranto
|passage=But come, Lady, we are too near the '''mouth''' of the cavern; let us seek its inmost recesses.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=1|passage=‘It was called the wickedest street in London and the entrance was just here. I imagine the '''mouth''' of the road lay between this lamp standard and the second from the next down there.’}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 August 26|author=Tim Dunn|title=Great railway bores of our time!|journal=Rail|page=42|text=But why give a tunnel '''mouth''' any decoration whatsoever?}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[loud]] or overly [[talkative]] person.
#: {{ux|en|My kid sister is a real '''mouth'''; she never shuts up.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[gossip]].
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2012|author=w:Stuart Carolan|actor=w:Killian Scott|role=Tommy Daly|title={{w|Love/Hate (TV series)|Love/Hate}}|season=3|number=3|time=40:45|text=Siobhán, you know Donna's a '''mouth'''.}}
# {{lb|en|saddlery}} The [[crosspiece]] of a [[bridle]] [[bit]], which enters the mouth of an animal.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[principal]] [[speaker]]; one who utters the common opinion; a [[mouthpiece]].
#* {{RQ:Spectator|IV|403|12 June 1712|passage=Every coffeehouse has some particular statesman belonging to it, who is the '''mouth''' of the street where he lives.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Speech; language; testimony.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|18|16|passage=that in the '''mouth''' of two or three witnesses every word may be established}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A wry face; a grimace; a mow.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Midsummer|III|ii|passage=Counterfeit sad looks, / Make '''mouths''' upon me when I turn my back.}}

